{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityMeromorphic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityMeromorphic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.DoublyPeriodicLiouville","lean:module:QOU.Common.PeriodicDense"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityMeromorphic.uniqueUpToScalar_of_ratio_dense_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityMeromorphic.uniqueUpToScalar_of_ratio_dense_periodic","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevRigidityMeromorphic.lean#L87-L120","doc":"**Sharper reduction — periodicity only on a dense set (bricks b/c internalized).**\nThe existing `FaddeevPhi` ratio lemmas (`CyclicDilogPentagon.ratio_ib_periodic`,\n`ratio_ibinv_periodic`) give the two periodicities of `r = Ψ/Φ` only **where the\nshared quasi-period prefactor is nonzero** — a *dense* locus, not all of `ℂ`. This\ntheorem consumes exactly that: `r` entire, and `r` periodic under each basis vector\non a **dense** set `Sᵢ`. The merged dense-extension core\n(`QOU.Common.periodic_of_continuous_of_eqOn_dense`) promotes each dense-set\nperiodicity to everywhere (a continuous function periodic on a dense set is periodic\neverywhere), then `uniqueUpToScalar_meromorphic` finishes.\n\nAfter this, the **sole** genuinely-open analytic input for the meromorphic `Φ_b` is\n`hr_entire` — that `r` extends across the removable singularities to an entire\nfunction (the divisor-rigidity fact bricks b/c name). The periodicity is no longer an\ninput: it is derived from the difference equations on the dense prefactor-nonzero\nlocus and promoted by continuity. Density of that locus is a discreteness fact about\n`Φ_b`'s zero/pole lattice, folded into the `Dense Sᵢ` hypotheses and gated — like\n`hr_entire` — on the `PhiBProd` construction; neither is axiomatized here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityMeromorphic.ratio_const_meromorphic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityMeromorphic.ratio_const_meromorphic","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevRigidityMeromorphic.lean#L72-L85","doc":"**Corollary — proportionality of the entire ratio itself.** Under the same\nhypotheses the ratio `r` is the constant `c`, so on the nonvanishing locus of `Φ`\nthe two solutions agree up to that one scalar. This is the form fed back into the\n`FaddeevPhi` rigidity statement once bricks (b/c) pin `hr_entire` for `Φ_b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityMeromorphic.uniqueUpToScalar_meromorphic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityMeromorphic.uniqueUpToScalar_meromorphic","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevRigidityMeromorphic.lean#L49-L70","doc":"**Route-B brick (d): meromorphic rigidity assembly from the entire ratio.**\nLet `Φ, Ψ : ℂ → ℂ` be the two meromorphic solutions and `r` their ratio\n(`r z = Ψ z / Φ z` wherever `Φ z ≠ 0`). If\n\n* `r` is **entire** (`hr_entire`) — the open divisor-rigidity input (bricks b/c),\n  *not* derivable from the difference equations (the elliptic ratio can be\n  nonconstant); and\n* `r` is periodic under both vectors of an `ℝ`-basis `bas` of `ℂ` (`hper`) — the\n  double periodicity from route-B step 2 plus the dense-extension core,\n\nthen `∃ c, Ψ z = c · Φ z` for every `z` with `Φ z ≠ 0`. The doubly-periodic-entire\nLiouville lemma supplies the constancy of `r`; proportionality is derived. ","signatureChunk":0}]}